{
  "name": "Jester's Falling Star Musket",
  "category": "combat",
  "concept": {
    "literalSynthesis": "The jester's star musket fires with a fallen star as its ammunition; a successful hit sends a smaller, trailing star back into the fight.",
    "coreMechanic": "Fire one gravity-arching ranged shot at a time, consuming one fallen-star ammunition unit for each accepted primary shot. A hit releases one separate, slower star that gradually homes toward nearby enemies. The musket's 31 base damage and 0.533-second use interval retain the generated musket's basic shot profile; the follow-up adds a modest 10-damage hit when it connects. The weapon is single-stack and reusable, but its ammunition is a recurring cost. The fallen star's own damage is a source ammunition contribution, not evidence of a standalone weapon attack.",
    "parentAContribution": "The generated parent's identity is a Jester's Star Musket, with ranged damage 31, 5.25 knockback, a 32-tick firing interval, and a star projectile. Its useful contribution is the musket's deliberate, measured shot cadence and ranged punch; the new primary trajectory and follow-up are authored mechanics.",
    "parentBContribution": "The other parent is Terraria's Fallen Star, a consumable material and fallen-star ammo category with a large stack size. It supplies the actual native ammunition requirement and the identity of the small follow-up star; its negative damage sentinel is not treated as an attack value.",
    "playerExperience": "Aim and fire at the cursor. Each shot spends a fallen star; direct hits can release one low-damage homing follow-up. Gravity makes the main shot arc, while the follow-up's slow steering helps it pursue nearby targets.",
    "plannedPlayerActions": [
      {
        "input": "primary_use",
        "intent": "Aim at a target and fire a single gravity-arching musket shot, consuming one fallen star. A hit releases one separate, slowly homing star."
      }
    ]
  },
  "realization": {
    "description": "A reusable ranged musket that consumes one fallen star per shot. Its cursor-aimed main projectile follows a gravity arc; on a hit, it releases a separate star that slowly homes toward nearby enemies. The follow-up is a separate projectile and is not guaranteed to hit.",
    "playerExperience": "The 32-tick base firing interval is deliberate, and ammunition is the recurring cost. The main shot deals 31 base damage; a hit can add one 10-damage follow-up if the slower star connects."
  },
